```

# 5. Linux File Permissions

Linux uses three primary permissions:

| Permission | Meaning | Numeric value |
|---|---|---|
| Read (`r`) | Read file contents | 4 |
| Write (`w`) | Modify file contents | 2 |
| Execute (`x`) | Execute a file | 1 |

Permission groups:

- User (u)
- Group (g)
- Others (o)

### Important commands

```bash
ls -l
chmod 755 script.sh
chmod 744 file.txt
chmod u+x script.sh
chmod go-w file.txt
chown username file.txt
chown username:group file.txt
```

Example:

`chmod 755 script.sh`

- Owner: Read, Write, Execute
- Group: Read, Execute
- Others: Read, Execute

