# 7. Process Management

A process is a running program or service. Every process has a Process ID (PID).

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `ps` | Displays running processes |
| `ps aux` | Displays detailed process information |
| `top` | Monitors running processes |
| `htop` | Interactive process monitor |
| `kill PID` | Sends termination signal |
| `kill -9 PID` | Forcefully terminates a process |
| `jobs` | Displays background jobs |
| `bg` | Runs a suspended job in background |
| `fg` | Brings a job to foreground |
| `pgrep` | Searches for process IDs |
| `pkill` | Terminates processes by name |

Examples:

```bash
ps
ps aux
top
htop

pgrep firefox
kill 1234
jobs
```

Replace `1234` with the actual process ID.

